<title>BELGIUM: Parliament supports EU ban on meat hormones.</title>
<headline>Parliament supports EU ban on meat hormones.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Parliament on Thursday urged the European Commission to defy pressure from the United States and other countries and to use all legal means to maintain a ban on imports of hormone-treated meat.</p>
<p>It said that a preliminary World Trade Organisation panel ruling against the EU ban was unacceptable and urged the Commission to put forward to the WTO new scientific data showing the risks of meat hormones.</p>
<p>It also called for stricter controls to ensure that all member states respect the ban on sales of hormone treated-meat.</p>
<p>EU Industry Commissioner Martin Bangemann told the parliament that the Commission would do everything possible within WTO rules to decide the appropriate level of food safety for EU citizens.</p>
<p>The WTO is due to issue a final report by the end of June.</p>
</text>
